AB  - Conidium is the main infection unit and reproductive unit of pathogenic fungi. Exploring the mechanism of conidiation and its regulation contributes to understanding the pathogenicity of pathogenic fungi. Vib-1, a transcription factor, was reported to participate in the conidiation process. However, the regulation mechanism of Vib-1 in conidiation is still unclear. In this study, we analyzed the function of Vib-1 and its regulation mechanism in conidiation through knocking out and overexpression of Vib-1 in entomopathogenic fungus Metarhizium acridum. Results showed that the colonial growth of Mavib-1 disruption mutant (Mavib-1) was significantly decreased, and conidiation was earlier compared to wild type (WT), while overexpression of Mavib-1 led to a delayed conidiation especially when carbon or nitrogen sources were insufficient. Overexpression of Mavib-1 resulted in a conidiation pattern shift from microcycle conidiation to normal conidiation on nutrient-limited medium. These results indicated that Mavib-1 acted as a positive regulator in vegetative growth and a negative regulator in conidiation by affecting utilization of carbon and nitrogen sources in M. acridum. Transcription profile analysis demonstrated that many genes related to carbon and nitrogen source metabolisms were differentially expressed in Mavib-1 and OE strains compared to WT. Moreover, Mavib-1 affects the conidial germi
